%N A399008 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of inequivalent ways to place k non-attacking rooks on an n X n board up to rectangular symmetries of the board.
%H A399008 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A399008/b399008.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1325</a> (rows 0..50)
%e A399008 Triangle begins:
%e A399008   1;
%e A399008   1,  1;
%e A399008   1,  1,   1;
%e A399008   1,  4,   5,    2;
%e A399008   1,  4,  20,   24,     8;
